{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "An Emotional Week", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Enough Is Enough", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Relate information about common solutions to problems in spoken or written documents. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "What Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You change emphasis from the beginning  of the sentence to another part of the sentence when you use <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> and <span class=\"italic\">who</span> phrases as subjects.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Usually, you focus on the subject - that is the person or thing that is doing the action. <br/>  Example: <span class=\"italic\">Joan told a hilarious joke.</span><br/>(Joan does the action.)<br/><br/> When you want to emphasize a different part of the sentence, you isolate that part and we put the rest of the information into a <span class=\"italic\">what</span>-phrase (or a <span class=\"italic\">that</span>-clause.)<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">What was hilarious, was the joke Joan told.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">That</span> with the subject  from the original sentence becomes the subordinated content clause. This clause functions as the subject of a sentence.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">That she imitated our teacher was funny.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">What</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Who</span> begins the noun phrase. The effect is that more emphasis is placed on other information.<br/> Example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">What was hilarious was her imitation of the teacher.</span><br/>        <span class=\"italic\"> Who she should have made fun of was the principal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "That I haven't completely lost it is a miracle!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What she needs is to increase her emotional intelligence.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What she thought is that I was criticizing her.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What she said was that I was wasting her time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Who I have to feel good about helping is myself! ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Tag Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A tag question is a short question that comes at the end of  a statement.<br/> It is often used when we want to:<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"strong\">confirm whether or not something is true</span>, or</li> <li><span class=\"strong\">to get a reply</span> from someone we are speaking to.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement comes before a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> tag question.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'yes'.<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement comes before a positive tag question.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'no'.<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were</span> you? </li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak Spanish, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal</span> verb, the tag will be the same.<br/> For all other main verbs, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do/does</span> or <span class=\"italic\">did/didn't</span>.<br/><br/> Look at the examples in the chart:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He likes \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You liked \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You haven't told off someone else on the bus, have you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You didn't tell her that, did you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm not deranged, am I?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She didn't want to listen, did she? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's her loss, isn't it?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tell someone off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to reprimand or scold someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You haven't told off someone else on the bus, have you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about reactions and behavior in different situations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be all ears", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to be ready to listen to something that someone is going to say", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm all ears.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "deranged", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unable to think or act in a normal or logical way ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm not deranged, am I?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lose it", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become very angry or emotionally upset", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That I haven't completely lost it is a miracle!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to achieve", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to reach something by working hard", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When people have emotional intelligence, they function better and achieve more in the work environment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "resistant ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "opposed to something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She was really resistant to hearing what I had to say.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "insignificant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "small or unimportant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She made me feel really insignificant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "receptive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "willing to listen or accept ideas", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She doesn't seem like she's very receptive to change.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On the Internet, watch a movie or TV show with a lot of dialogue between two people.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose a dialogue section that is about 20 seconds long.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to the section as many times as you need.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the dialogue using reported speech.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading the dialogue aloud with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about reactions and behavior.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I shift emphasis by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">that</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for clarification and confirmation. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I transcribe a dialogue in reported speech.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn9le04ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le04ob10re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn9le04ob10re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn9le04ob10re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Hello?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: That's it! Enough is enough!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sally! What's wrong? You haven't told off someone else on the bus, have you?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Ha ha. No. But my week is the pits. That I haven't completely lost it is a miracle!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Get it all off your chest. I'm all ears. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: So I met with my boss and I printed some information about emotional intelligence and I gave it to her. What she needs is to increase her emotional intelligence.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn9le04ob10re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You didn't tell her that, did you?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: No! I'm not deranged, am I?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: So how did she respond to you? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Not well. What she thought was that I was criticizing her. I tried to explain the concept and that when people have emotional intelligence, they function better and achieve more in the work environment.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: She didn't want to listen, did she? She doesn't seem like she's very receptive to change.", "time": "28000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn9le04ob10re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: No. She was really resistant to what I had to say. She made me feel really insignificant. In fact, what she said was that I was wasting her time. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sally, the important thing is that you are making an effort to improve yourself. You attempted to share your enthusiasm with the wrong person. It's her loss, isn't it?  You just have to let it go.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: You're right. Who I have to feel good about is helping myself! <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: That's the spirit!", "time": "55000", "id": 3}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can write about  reactions and behavior.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can shift emphasis by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">that</span>. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can ask for clarification and confirmation. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What is the best way to deal with criticism from your boss?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What is constructive criticism and how can it be beneficial?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Criticism is hard to take.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Sally says <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">enough is enough</span>!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}, {"content": [{"content": "We say <span class=\"italic\">\u201cenough is enough\u201d</span> when we can't tolerate any more of something.", "tip_id": 0, "type": "text"}], "type": "tips"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.", "type": "text"}]}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct": 0, "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct": 1, "id": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nSally's week has been <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_2_0\">the pits</span>.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Activity 1", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "You are done!", "attempt_feedback"